## Usage Guide

### Writing Your First Program

1. Open the simulator and type your assembly code in the **Editor** tab.
2. Click **Assemble (F8)** to compile. Check the **Console** tab for errors.
3. Click **Run (F5)** to execute continuously, or **Step (F6)** to execute one instruction at a time.
4. View results in the **Registers** panel, **Flags** panel, or **Memory Viewer**.

### Basic Program Structure

Every program typically follows this pattern:

```asm
; Comments start with a semicolon
    ORG 2000H           ; Set the starting address of the program

    ; Your instructions go here
    MVI A, 25H          ; Load a value into accumulator
    STA 3000H           ; Store result at memory address 3000H
    HLT                 ; Stop execution

; Data section
    ORG 2050H           ; Set the address for data
    DB 05H, 0AH, 0FH   ; Define bytes in memory
```

### Trainer Kit Mode

Use the **hex keypad** to enter addresses and data directly into memory, just like a real hardware trainer kit:

1. Enter the memory address using hex keys.
2. Press the appropriate function key to examine/modify memory.
3. Use the 7-segment display to view addresses and data values.

