## Registers & Flags

### 8-bit Registers

| Register | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| **A**    | Accumulator — primary register for arithmetic/logic operations |
| **B**    | General purpose register (pairs with C) |
| **C**    | General purpose register (pairs with B) |
| **D**    | General purpose register (pairs with E) |
| **E**    | General purpose register (pairs with D) |
| **H**    | General purpose register (pairs with L, forms memory address) |
| **L**    | General purpose register (pairs with H, forms memory address) |
| **M**    | Not a real register — refers to the memory location pointed to by **HL** |

### 16-bit Register Pairs

| Pair      | Registers | Usage |
|-----------|-----------|-------|
| **B**     | B and C   | General purpose pair |
| **D**     | D and E   | General purpose pair |
| **H**     | H and L   | Memory pointer pair |
| **SP**    | —         | Stack Pointer (16-bit) |
| **PSW**   | A + Flags | Program Status Word (used with PUSH/POP) |

### Flags

The 8085 has 5 status flags that are set/cleared based on the result of operations:

| Flag | Name            | Set When (= 1) |
|------|-----------------|-----------------|
| **S**  | Sign          | Bit 7 of the result is 1 (result is negative) |
| **Z**  | Zero          | Result is zero |
| **AC** | Auxiliary Carry | There is a carry from bit 3 to bit 4 |
| **P**  | Parity        | Result has an even number of 1-bits |
| **CY** | Carry         | There is a carry or borrow from bit 7 |

