## Complete Instruction Set Reference

### Data Transfer Instructions

These instructions move data between registers, memory, and I/O ports without modifying flags.

| Instruction        | Operation                              | Description |
|--------------------|----------------------------------------|-------------|
| `MOV r1, r2`       | r1 ← r2                               | Copy register r2 to r1 |
| `MVI r, data`      | r ← data                              | Load immediate 8-bit data to register |
| `LDA addr`         | A ← [addr]                            | Load accumulator from memory address |
| `STA addr`         | [addr] ← A                            | Store accumulator to memory address |
| `LHLD addr`        | L ← [addr], H ← [addr+1]             | Load HL pair from memory |
| `SHLD addr`        | [addr] ← L, [addr+1] ← H             | Store HL pair to memory |
| `LXI rp, d16`      | rp ← d16                              | Load 16-bit immediate to register pair |
| `LDAX rp`          | A ← [rp]                              | Load A from address in rp (B or D only) |
| `STAX rp`          | [rp] ← A                              | Store A to address in rp (B or D only) |
| `XCHG`             | DE ↔ HL                               | Exchange DE and HL pairs |

### Arithmetic Instructions

These instructions perform addition, subtraction, and increment/decrement. They affect all flags unless noted.

| Instruction        | Operation                              | Description |
|--------------------|----------------------------------------|-------------|
| `ADD r`            | A ← A + r                             | Add register to A |
| `ADC r`            | A ← A + r + CY                        | Add register to A with carry |
| `SUB r`            | A ← A − r                             | Subtract register from A |
| `SBB r`            | A ← A − r − CY                        | Subtract register from A with borrow |
| `INR r`            | r ← r + 1                             | Increment register by 1 |
| `DCR r`            | r ← r − 1                             | Decrement register by 1 |
| `INX rp`           | rp ← rp + 1                           | Increment register pair (no flags affected) |
| `DCX rp`           | rp ← rp − 1                           | Decrement register pair (no flags affected) |
| `DAD rp`           | HL ← HL + rp                          | Add register pair to HL (only CY affected) |
| `DAA`              | Decimal adjust A                       | Adjust A for BCD addition |
| `ADI data`         | A ← A + data                          | Add immediate to A |
| `ACI data`         | A ← A + data + CY                     | Add immediate to A with carry |
| `SUI data`         | A ← A − data                          | Subtract immediate from A |
| `SBI data`         | A ← A − data − CY                     | Subtract immediate from A with borrow |

### Logical Instructions

These instructions perform bitwise operations, comparisons, and rotations.

| Instruction        | Operation                              | Description |
|--------------------|----------------------------------------|-------------|
| `ANA r`            | A ← A AND r                           | Logical AND register with A |
| `XRA r`            | A ← A XOR r                           | Logical XOR register with A |
| `ORA r`            | A ← A OR r                            | Logical OR register with A |
| `CMP r`            | Compare A with r                       | Sets flags based on A − r, **A is unchanged** |
| `ANI data`         | A ← A AND data                        | AND immediate with A |
| `XRI data`         | A ← A XOR data                        | XOR immediate with A |
| `ORI data`         | A ← A OR data                         | OR immediate with A |
| `CPI data`         | Compare A with data                    | Sets flags based on A − data, **A is unchanged** |
| `RLC`              | Rotate A left                          | Bit 7 → CY and bit 0 |
| `RRC`              | Rotate A right                         | Bit 0 → CY and bit 7 |
| `RAL`              | Rotate A left through carry            | 9-bit rotate: bit 7 → CY, old CY → bit 0 |
| `RAR`              | Rotate A right through carry           | 9-bit rotate: bit 0 → CY, old CY → bit 7 |
| `CMA`              | A ← NOT A                             | 1's complement of A |
| `CMC`              | CY ← NOT CY                           | Complement carry flag |
| `STC`              | CY ← 1                                | Set carry flag |

### Branch Instructions

These instructions change the flow of execution. Conditional branches check flag values.

| Instruction        | Condition            | Description |
|--------------------|----------------------|-------------|
| `JMP addr`         | —                    | Jump unconditionally |
| `JC addr`          | CY = 1               | Jump if carry |
| `JNC addr`         | CY = 0               | Jump if no carry |
| `JZ addr`          | Z = 1                | Jump if zero |
| `JNZ addr`         | Z = 0                | Jump if not zero |
| `JP addr`          | S = 0                | Jump if positive |
| `JM addr`          | S = 1                | Jump if minus (negative) |
| `JPE addr`         | P = 1                | Jump if parity even |
| `JPO addr`         | P = 0                | Jump if parity odd |
| `CALL addr`        | —                    | Call subroutine (push PC, jump to addr) |
| `RET`              | —                    | Return from subroutine (pop PC) |
| `PCHL`             | —                    | Jump to address in HL (PC ← HL) |
| `RST n`            | —                    | Restart: call address n×8 (n = 0–7) |

**Conditional CALL variants:** `CC`, `CNC`, `CZ`, `CNZ`, `CP`, `CM`, `CPE`, `CPO`
**Conditional RET variants:** `RC`, `RNC`, `RZ`, `RNZ`, `RP`, `RM`, `RPE`, `RPO`

### Stack & I/O Instructions

| Instruction        | Operation                              | Description |
|--------------------|----------------------------------------|-------------|
| `PUSH rp`          | Stack ← rp                            | Push register pair onto stack |
| `POP rp`           | rp ← Stack                            | Pop register pair from stack |
| `XTHL`             | (SP) ↔ HL                             | Exchange top of stack with HL |
| `SPHL`             | SP ← HL                               | Load SP from HL |
| `IN port`          | A ← port                              | Read from input port into A |
| `OUT port`         | port ← A                              | Write A to output port |

> **rp** can be **B** (BC), **D** (DE), **H** (HL), or **PSW** (A + Flags)

### Control Instructions

| Instruction | Description |
|-------------|-------------|
| `NOP`       | No operation (does nothing, wastes 1 cycle) |
| `HLT`       | Halt processor — stops execution |
| `EI`        | Enable interrupts |
| `DI`        | Disable interrupts |
| `RIM`       | Read interrupt mask into A |
| `SIM`       | Set interrupt mask from A |

