## Tips & Common Patterns

### Storing an Array in Memory

Use `ORG` to set the address and `DB` to define the data:

```asm
    ORG 2050H
    DB 05H               ; Count (optional, but useful)
    DB 11H, 22H, 33H, 44H, 55H   ; Array elements
```

### Looping Through an Array

Use `HL` as a pointer and `C` as a counter:

```asm
    LXI H, 2051H        ; Point HL to first element
    MVI C, 05H           ; Load count

LOOP:
    MOV A, M             ; Load current element into A
    ; ... do something with A ...
    INX H                ; Move to next element
    DCR C                ; Decrement counter
    JNZ LOOP             ; Repeat if not zero
```

### Comparing Two Numbers

`CMP` subtracts without changing A, only sets flags:

```asm
    MOV A, M             ; Load first value
    INX H
    CMP M                ; Compare A with next value
    JC LESS              ; Jump if A < M[HL]  (Carry = 1)
    JZ EQUAL             ; Jump if A == M[HL] (Zero = 1)
    ; otherwise A > M[HL]
```

### Using the Stack

Always initialize SP before using `PUSH`, `POP`, or `CALL`:

```asm
    LXI SP, 20FFH       ; Stack grows downward from 20FFH
    PUSH B               ; Save BC on stack
    ; ... do work ...
    POP B                ; Restore BC
```

